==History==
2017
*The Zappies [[Cards|card]] was added to the game on 12/12/2017, in the [[Version History#Electrifying Update (12/12/2017)|Electrifying Update]] {{Balance|Add}}.
2018 
*On 24/1/2018, a [[Version History#Balance Changes (24/1/2018)|Balance Update]], allowed the Zappies to target air [[:Category:Troop Cards|troops]] {{Balance|Neutral}}.
*On 3/9/2018, a [[Version History#Balance Changes (3/9/2018)|Balance Update]], increasing the Zappies' first attack time interval to 1.4 seconds (from 0.6 second) {{Balance|Nerf}}, but changed their attack so that it cannot be reset by stunning cards {{Balance|Neutral}}.
*On 5/9/2018, the [[Version History#September%202018%20Update%20(5/9/2018)|September 2018 Update]], changed it so that {{Rarity|Rare}} cards start at Level 3 and end at Level 13 (from 1 to 11) {{Balance|Neutral}}.
2019
*On 15/4/2019, the [[Version History#April%202019%20Update%20(15/4/2019)|April 2019 Update]], added an extra [[Star Points|Star Level]] {{Balance|Add}}.
*On 26/11/2019, the [[Version History#End%20of%20November%202019%20Update%20(26/11/2019)|End of November 2019 Update]] added a card render to the Zappies' card info screen {{Balance|Add}}.
2020 
*On 4/2/2020, a [[Version History#Balance Changes (4/2/2020)|Balance Update]], increased the Zappies’ damage by 20% {{Balance|Buff}}, but also increased their attack time interval to 2 seconds (from 1.6 seconds) {{Balance|Nerf}}, decreased their first attack time interval to 1 second (from 1.4 seconds) {{Balance|Buff}}, and increased the deploy stagger for each Zappy to 0.15 seconds (from 0.1 seconds) {{Balance|Nerf}}.
*On 2/6/2020, a [[Version History#Balance Changes (2/6/2020)|Balance Update]], decreased the deploy stagger for each Zappy to 0.1 seconds (from 0.15 seconds) {{Balance|Buff}}.
*On 7/7/2020, a [[Version History#Balance Changes (7/7/2020)|Balance Update]], increased the Zappies' damage by 14% {{Balance|Buff}}, but increased their attack time interval to 2.1 seconds (from 2 seconds) {{Balance|Nerf}}, and increased their first attack time interval to 1.1 seconds (from 1 second) {{Balance|Nerf}}.
*On 9/9/2020, a [[Version History#Balance Changes (9/9/2020)|Balance Update]], decreased the Zappies' first attack time interval to 0.9 seconds (from 1.1 seconds) {{Balance|Buff}}.
2021
*On 30/3/2021, the [[Version History#2021%20Quarter%201%20Update%20(30/3/2021)|2021 Quarter 1 Update]], increased the Zappies' first attack time interval to 1.1 seconds (from 0.9 seconds) {{Balance|Nerf}}.
*On 27/10/2021, the [[Version History#Champions%20Update%20(27/10/2021)|Champions Update]], increased the level cap of all cards to 14 (from 13) {{Balance|Buff}}.
*On 1/11/2021, an [[Version History#Optional%20Update%20(1/11/2021)|Optional Update]], made it so that the [[Mega Knight]] cannot be forever stunned by Zappies {{Balance|Neutral}}.
2022
*On 26/10/2022, the [[Version History#2022%20Quarter%203%20Update%20(26/10/2022)|2022 Quarter 3 Update]], moved the [[Arenas|Arena]] to unlock the Zappies from Electro Valley to Hog Mountain {{Balance|Buff}}.
2023
*On 19/6/2023, the [[Version History#Card%20Evolution%20Update%20(19/6/2023)|Card Evolution Update]], increased the Level cap of all cards to 15 (from 14) {{Balance|Buff}}.
2025
*On 31/3/2025, the [[Version History#2025 Quarter 1 Update (31/3/2025)|2025 Quarter 1 Update]], decreased the Zappies' hitpoints by 0.18% and increased their damage by 0.86% {{Balance|Buff}}.
*On 4/8/2025, the [[Version History/2025#Pass Royale and more (4/8/2025)|August 2025 Update]] decreased the Zappies' first attack time interval to 0.8 seconds (from 1.1 seconds) {{Balance|Buff}}.
2026

* On 4/8/2026, a Balance Update, increased the Zappies' hit speed to 2.2 seconds (from 2.1 seconds)

